          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamics"} dynamics
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+system"} physical system
            may be encoded by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonlinear+functional"} nonlinear functional
            – called the
            %strong action functional
            – on its
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} configuration space
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mechanics"} classical mechanics
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical field theory
                – by the
                %strong action principle
                or
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+least+action"} principle of least action
                – the extrema of the action functional – obtained by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variational calculus
                and given by
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equation"} Euler-Lagrange equation
            %li
              %p
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
                the evolution of the
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} quantum state
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
                – of the exponentiated action functional over the space of field configurations.
          %p
            For emphasis the description of dynamics by action functionals is called the
            %strong Lagrangean
            approach. Another formulation of dynamics in physics that does not involve an action functional explicitly is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+mechanics"} Hamiltonian mechanics
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            in terms of action functionals suffers from a lack of precise understanding of what the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            over the action functional really means.
          %div{:style => "margin: 0px 10px 10px 0px; float: left"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:alt => "Action functional on a napkin", :src => "/nlab/files/action_functional_on_a_napkin.jpg"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"} Taken from A Zee, Fearful Symmetry
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            be the ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
            and equipped with an additive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuum"} continuum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+object"} line object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}^1
            (see there). Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \in \mathbf{H}
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} configuration space
            of a physical system. Then an
            %strong action functional
            is a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mi ℏ
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar} S(-)) : C \to \mathbb{A}^1 / \mathbb{Z}
                  \\,
          %p
            (here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℏ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
            refers to
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck%27s+constant"} Planck's constant
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            then there is an
            %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/cohesive+(infinity,1)-topos+--+structures#CurvatureCharacteristics"} intrinsic differential
            of the action functional to a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mi ℏ
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{d} \exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar} S(-)) : C \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR}\mathbb{A}^1/\mathbb{Z}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation"} equation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mi ℏ
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{d} \exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar} S(-)) = 0
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equation"} Euler-Lagrange equation
            of the system. It characterizes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/critical+locus"} critical locus
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            inside the configuration space: the space of classically realized trajectories/histories of the system. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
            then this critical locus is presented by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST-BV+complex"} BRST-BV complex
          %h3#LocalActionFunctional Local action functionals (traditional theory)
          %p
            An action functional is called
            %strong local
            if it arises from integration of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian"} Lagrangian
          %p
            In traditional theory this is interpreted as follows: an action functional
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S : C \to \mathbb{A}^1
            is called local if
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} configuration space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is the space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = \Gamma_X(E)
                of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
                over some parameter space (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                = succeed ");" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p
                there is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian"} Lagrangian
                density
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mrow
                          %mi dim
                          %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_\infty(E) \to \Omega^{\dim X}(X)
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %li
              %p
                on a section/field configuration
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : X \to E
                the action
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                takes the value
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi X
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      S(\phi) = \int_X L(j_\infty(\phi))
                      \\,,
              %p
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi i
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_\infty(\phi) = (\phi, \partial_i \phi, \cdots)
                is the jet-prolongation of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                (the collection of all its higher partial derivatives).
          %p
            Consider action functional on a configuration space of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p We can consider
          %ol
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi q
                      %mo ˙
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(q) = \int_a^b L(q,\dot{q}) \,\mathrm{d}t
              , where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              is a path through configuration space, on the time interval
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [a,b]
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi q
                        %mo ˙
                      %mo =
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dot{q} = \mathrm{d}q/\mathrm{d}t
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q(a)
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q(b)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi q
                      %mo ˙
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi S
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi q
                      %mo ˙
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(q,\dot{q}) = \int_{S} \mathcal{L}(q,\dot{q}) \,\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}y\,\mathrm{d}z
              , where now
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              is a configuration of fields on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              (typically that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi q
                      %mo ˙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dot{q}
              go to zero if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is all of space).
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi R
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi q
                      %mo ˙
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi z
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(q) = \int_{R} \mathcal{L}(q,\dot{q}) \,\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}y\,\mathrm{d}z\,\mathrm{d}t
              , where now
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              is a configuration of fields on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi q
                        %mo ˙
                      %mo =
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dot{q} = \partial{q}/\partial{t}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            The formulation of (3) above is still not manifestly coordinate independent. However,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi x
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi z
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}y\,\mathrm{d}z\,\mathrm{d}t
            is simply the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+form"} volume form
            on spacetime and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi q
                    %mo ˙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dot{q}
            is merely one choice of coordinate on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} state space
            and could just as easily be replaced by a derivative with respect to any timelike coordinate on spacetime (or drop coordinates altogether).
          %h3#ExtendedLocalInGaugeTheory Extended local action functionals in (higher) gauge theory
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theories"} gauge theories
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theories"} higher gauge theories
            the configuration spaces of the physical system are in general not plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            or similar, but are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            or more generally
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoids"} smooth groupoids
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth ∞-groupoids
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"} geometry of physics
          %p
            For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
            the smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            (see at
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection on a bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoid"} smooth groupoid
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            configurations is the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+stack"} mapping stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma, \mathbf{B}G_{conn}] \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            (or some concretification thereof, see at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "geometry%20of%20physics#DifferentialModuli"} geometric of physics – differential moduli
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoid"} smooth groupoid
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-configurations" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connections
            on
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            over
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
            between these. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+space"} infinitesimal
            approximation to this
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebroid"} ∞-Lie algebroid
            is the (off-shell)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
            of the theory. The tangent to the
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+transformations"} higher gauge transformations
            becomes the
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %em ghosts
            in the BRST complex.
          %p
            More generally
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            here can by any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-group"} smooth ∞-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-group"} circle n-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^{n-1}U(1)
            or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+2-group"} String 2-group
            or the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fivebrane+6-group"} Fivebrane 6-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma, \mathbf{B}G_{conn}]
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher gauge field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
            between these,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+transformations"} higher gauge transformations
            between those, and so on.
          %p
            Notice that this means in particular that in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            is not just a plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            but is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of gauge field configurations.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+invariance"} gauge invariant
            action functional is then a morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth ∞-groupoids
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp( i S(-)) \colon [\Sigma, \mathbf{B}G_{conn}] \to U(1)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is of particular interest, again, if it is
            = succeed "." do
              %em local
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+topological+quantum+field+theory"} extended topological quantum field theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+bundle"} prequantum bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+n-bundle"} prequantum n-bundle
          %p
            This is notably the case for all (higher) gauge theories of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/infinity-Chern-Simons+theory"} infinity-Chern-Simons theory
            type, such as ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            and such as ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(i S(-)) \colon [\Sigma, \mathbf{B}G_{conn}]
            arises itself from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+Lagrangian"} extended Lagrangian
            that is defined on the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of gauge field configurations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
            itself, namely from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+characteristic+class"} universal characteristic class
            in higher nonabelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{L} \colon \mathbf{B}G_{conn} \to \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}
            is the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+infinity-stack"} moduli infinity-stack
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+form"} Chern-Simons form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CS
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CS(A)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-group"} circle (n-1)-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
            and accordingly acts globally on the connection. This is hence a fully local
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian"} Lagrangian
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+Lagrangian"} extended Lagrangian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+circle+n-bundle"} prequantum circle n-bundle
            on the universal moduli stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
            itself.
          %p
            For instance for ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+group"} semisimple Lie group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            is a smooth and differential refinement of the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Pontryagin+class"} first Pontryagin class
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+Chern+class"} second Chern class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            may also be thought of as modulating the universal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            and this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+Lagrangian"} extended Lagrangian
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+Lagrangian"} extended Lagrangian
            becomes an extended action functional after
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+ordinary+differential+cohomology"} fiber integration in ordinary differential cohomology
            refines to a morphism of moduli stacks of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi k
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(2 \pi i \int_{\Sigma_k} (-))
                  \\colon
                  [\Sigma_k, \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{\mathrm{conn}} ]
                  \\to
                  \\mathbf{B}^{n-k}U(1)_{conn}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed manifold
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+n-form"} differential n-form
            to its ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+of+differential+forms"} integration of differential forms
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+holonomy"} higher holonomy
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
          %p
            Combining this with an extended
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian"} Lagrangian
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L} \colon \mathbf{B}G_{conn} \to \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}
            as above yields for each dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+circle+n-bundle"} prequantum circle n-bundle
            on the space of gauge field configurations over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mi π
                      %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi k
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(i S(-))
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\exp(2 \pi i \int_{\Sigma_k} [\Sigma_k, \mathbf{L}])
                  \\;\; \colon \;\;
                  [\Sigma_k, \mathbf{B}G_{conn}]
                  \\stackrel{[\Sigma_k, \mathbf{L}]}{\to}
                  [\Sigma_k, \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}]
                  \\stackrel{\exp(2 \pi i \int_{\Sigma_k}(-))}{\to}
                  \\mathbf{B}^{n-k}U(1)_{conn}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This morphism locally takes the local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            incarnation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} connection on an ∞-bundle
            to the exponentiation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+of+differential+forms"} integration of differential forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_\Sigma CS(A)
            of some higher
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+form"} Chern-Simons form
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+holonomy"} higher holonomy
            of the higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle n-bundle with connection
            over the universal moduli stack of fields, as modulated by the extended
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian"} Lagrangian
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
