          %h2#references References
          %p
            Historical and expository accounts of the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+extremal+action"}> principle of extremal action
            ” or “action principle”, for short:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Agamenon R. E. Oliveira,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em History of Two Fundamental Principles of Physics: Least Action and Conservation of Energy
                %strong 3
                2 (2014) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.4236/ahs.2014.32008"}> doi:10.4236/ahs.2014.32008
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Walter Dittrich,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Development of the Action Principle – A Didactic History from Euler-Lagrange to Schwinger
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-69105-9"} doi:10.1007/978-3-030-69105-9
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+Cline"}> Douglas Cline
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Variational Principles in Classical Mechanics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://classicalmechanics.lib.rochester.edu/pdf/Variational_Principles_in_Classical_Mechanics_3e_final_fbcover.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://phys.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Classical_Mechanics/Variational_Principles_in_Classical_Mechanics_(Cline)"} online version
          %p
            Textbook account in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theories"} gauge theories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Henneaux"}> Marc Henneaux
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Teitelboim"} Claudio Teitelboim
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantization+of+Gauge+Systems"} Quantization of Gauge Systems
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/books/paperback/9780691037691/quantization-of-gauge-systems"} ISBN:9780691037691
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/j.ctv10crg0r"} jstor:j.ctv10crg0r
          %p
            Lecture notes with more details are in the section
            %em
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics#LagrangiansAndActionFunctionals"} Lagrangians and Action functionals
            of
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"} geometry of physics
              \.
          %p
            Discussion of extended higher local action functional for (higher) gauge theories of generalized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            type are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Extended+higher+cup-product+Chern-Simons+theories"} Extended higher cup-product Chern-Simons theories
          %p
            The extended local action functionals for ordinary 3d
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
            and for 7d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+2-group"} String 2-group
            Chern-Simons theory are constructed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cech+cocycles+for+differential+characteristic+classes"} Cech cocycles for differential characteristic classes
          %p and discussed further in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/7d+Chern-Simons+theory+and+the+5-brane"} 7d Chern-Simons theory and the 5-brane
          %p A comprehensive discussion in a general context of higher differential geometry is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
